      {
        "path": "link_resolution_tests::nested::Str::leak",
        "kind": "function",
        "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/string/struct.String.html#method.leak",
        "docs": [
          {
            "type": "truncatedBlock",
            "nodes": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Consumes and leaks the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "String",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", returning a mutable reference to the contents,",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "&'a mut str",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ".",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "The caller has free choice over the returned lifetime, including ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "'static",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ". Indeed,",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "this function is ideally used for data that lives for the remainder of the program's life,",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "as dropping the returned reference will cause a memory leak.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "It does not reallocate or shrink the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "String",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", so the leaked allocation may include unused",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "capacity that is not part of the returned slice. If you want to discard excess capacity,",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "call ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "into_boxed_str",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/string/struct.String.html#method.into_boxed_str"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", and then ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Box::leak",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/boxed/struct.Box.html#method.leak"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " instead. However, keep in mind that",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "trimming the capacity may result in a reallocation and copy.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Title",
                "spans": [
