      {
        "path": "link_resolution_tests::HashSet",
        "kind": "struct",
        "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/collections/hash/set/struct.HashSet.html",
        "docs": [
          {
            "type": "truncatedBlock",
            "nodes": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "A ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "hash set",
                    "style": "Plain",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/index.html?search=std%3A%3Acollections"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " implemented as a ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "HashMap",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " where the value is ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "()",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ".",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "As with the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "HashMap",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/std/collections/hash/map/struct.HashMap.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " type, a ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "HashSet",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " requires that the elements",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "implement the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Eq",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/cmp/index.html?search=core%3A%3Acmp%3A%3AEq"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " and ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Hash",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/hash/index.html?search=core%3A%3Ahash%3A%3AHash"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " traits. This can frequently be achieved by",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "using ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "#[derive(PartialEq, Eq, Hash)]",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ". If you implement these yourself,",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "it is important that the following property holds:",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "text",
                "code": "k1 == k2 -> hash(k1) == hash(k2)\n"
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "In other words, if two keys are equal, their hashes must be equal.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Violating this property is a logic error.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "It is also a logic error for a key to be modified in such a way that the key's",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "hash, as determined by the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Hash",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/hash/index.html?search=core%3A%3Ahash%3A%3AHash"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " trait, or its equality, as determined by",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Eq",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/cmp/index.html?search=core%3A%3Acmp%3A%3AEq"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " trait, changes while it is in the map. This is normally only",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "possible through ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Cell",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/cell/index.html?search=core%3A%3Acell%3A%3ACell"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "RefCell",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/cell/index.html?search=core%3A%3Acell%3A%3ARefCell"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", global state, I/O, or unsafe code.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "The behavior resulting from either logic error is not specified, but will",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "be encapsulated to the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "HashSet",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " that observed the logic error and not",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "result in undefined behavior. This could include panics, incorrect results,",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "aborts, memory leaks, and non-termination.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Title",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Examples",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "use std::collections::HashSet;\n// Type inference lets us omit an explicit type signature (which\n// would be `HashSet<String>` in this example).\nlet mut books = HashSet::new();\n\n// Add some books.\nbooks.insert(\"A Dance With Dragons\".to_string());\nbooks.insert(\"To Kill a Mockingbird\".to_string());\nbooks.insert(\"The Odyssey\".to_string());\nbooks.insert(\"The Great Gatsby\".to_string());\n\n// Check for a specific one.\nif !books.contains(\"The Winds of Winter\") {\n    println!(\"We have {} books, but The Winds of Winter ain't one.\",\n             books.len());\n}\n\n// Remove a book.\nbooks.remove(\"The Odyssey\");\n\n// Iterate over everything.\nfor book in &books {\n    println!(\"{book}\");\n}"
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "The easiest way to use ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "HashSet",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " with a custom type is to derive",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Eq",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/cmp/index.html?search=core%3A%3Acmp%3A%3AEq"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " and ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Hash",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/hash/index.html?search=core%3A%3Ahash%3A%3AHash"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ". We must also derive ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "PartialEq",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/cmp/index.html?search=core%3A%3Acmp%3A%3APartialEq"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ",",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "which is required if ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Eq",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/cmp/index.html?search=core%3A%3Acmp%3A%3AEq"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " is derived.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "use std::collections::HashSet;\n#[derive(Hash, Eq, PartialEq, Debug)]\nstruct Viking {\n    name: String,\n    power: usize,\n}\n\nlet mut vikings = HashSet::new();\n\nvikings.insert(Viking { name: \"Einar\".to_string(), power: 9 });\nvikings.insert(Viking { name: \"Einar\".to_string(), power: 9 });\nvikings.insert(Viking { name: \"Olaf\".to_string(), power: 4 });\nvikings.insert(Viking { name: \"Harald\".to_string(), power: 8 });\n\n// Use derived implementation to print the vikings.\nfor x in &vikings {\n    println!(\"{x:?}\");\n}"
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "A ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "HashSet",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " with a known list of items can be initialized from an array:",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "use std::collections::HashSet;\n\nlet viking_names = HashSet::from([\"Einar\", \"Olaf\", \"Harald\"]);"
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Title",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Usage in ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "const",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " and ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "static",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Like ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "HashMap",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "HashSet",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " is randomly seeded: each ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "HashSet",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " instance uses a different seed,",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "which means that ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "HashSet::new",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " cannot be used in const context. To construct a ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "HashSet",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " in the",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "initializer of a ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "const",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " or ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "static",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " item, you will have to use a different hasher that does not",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "involve a random seed, as demonstrated in the following example. ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "A ",
                    "style": "Strong"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "HashSet",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
