              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Section",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Philosophy",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Markdown is intended to be as easy-to-read and easy-to-write as is feasible.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Readability, however, is emphasized above all else. A Markdown-formatted",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "document should be publishable as-is, as plain text, without looking",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "like it's been marked up with tags or formatting instructions. While",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Markdown's syntax has been influenced by several existing text-to-HTML",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "filters -- including ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Setext",
                    "style": "Plain",
                    "url": "http://docutils.sourceforge.net/mirror/setext.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "atx",
                    "style": "Plain",
                    "url": "http://www.aaronsw.com/2002/atx/"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Textile",
                    "style": "Plain",
                    "url": "http://textism.com/tools/textile/"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "reStructuredText",
                    "style": "Plain",
                    "url": "http://docutils.sourceforge.net/rst.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ",",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Grutatext",
                    "style": "Plain",
                    "url": "http://www.triptico.com/software/grutatxt.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", and ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "EtText",
                    "style": "Plain",
                    "url": "http://ettext.taint.org/doc/"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " -- the single biggest source of",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "inspiration for Markdown's syntax is the format of plain text email.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Section",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Block Elements",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Section",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Paragraphs and Line Breaks",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "A paragraph is simply one or more consecutive lines of text, separated",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "by one or more blank lines. (A blank line is any line that looks like a",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "blank line -- a line containing nothing but spaces or tabs is considered",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "blank.) Normal paragraphs should not be indented with spaces or tabs.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "The implication of the \"one or more consecutive lines of text\" rule is",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "that Markdown supports \"hard-wrapped\" text paragraphs. This differs",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "significantly from most other text-to-HTML formatters (including Movable",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Type's \"Convert Line Breaks\" option) which translate every line break",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "character in a paragraph into a ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "<br />",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " tag.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "When you ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "do",
                    "style": "Emphasis"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " want to insert a ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "<br />",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " break tag using Markdown, you",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "end a line with two or more spaces, then type return.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Section",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Headers",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Markdown supports two styles of headers, ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Setext",
                    "style": "Plain",
                    "url": "https://docs.rs/fixture-crate/latest/fixture-crate/index.html?search=fixture%2Dcrate%3A%3ASetext"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "1",
                    "style": "Plain",
                    "url": "https://docs.rs/fixture-crate/latest/fixture-crate/index.html?search=fixture%2Dcrate%3A%3A1"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " and ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "atx",
                    "style": "Plain",
                    "url": "https://docs.rs/fixture-crate/latest/fixture-crate/index.html?search=fixture%2Dcrate%3A%3Aatx"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "2",
                    "style": "Plain",
                    "url": "https://docs.rs/fixture-crate/latest/fixture-crate/index.html?search=fixture%2Dcrate%3A%3A2"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ".",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Optionally, you may \"close\" atx-style headers. This is purely",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "cosmetic -- you can use this if you think it looks better. The",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "closing hashes don't even need to match the number of hashes",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "used to open the header. (The number of opening hashes",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "determines the header level.)",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Section",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Blockquotes",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Markdown uses email-style ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ">",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " characters for blockquoting. If you're",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "familiar with quoting passages of text in an email message, then you",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "know how to create a blockquote in Markdown. It looks best if you hard",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "wrap the text and put a ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ">",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " before every line:",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "blockQuote",
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "type": "paragraph",
                    "spans": [
                      {
                        "text": "This is a blockquote with two paragraphs. Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet,",
