                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Vec",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " will never perform a \"small optimization\" where elements are actually",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "stored on the stack for two reasons:",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "list",
                "items": [
                  {
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "spans": [
                          {
                            "text": "It would make it more difficult for unsafe code to correctly manipulate",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "a ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "Vec",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": ". The contents of a ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "Vec",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " wouldn't have a stable address if it were",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "only moved, and it would be more difficult to determine if a ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "Vec",
                            "style": "InlineCode"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " had",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "actually allocated memory.",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "type": "paragraph",
                        "spans": [
                          {
                            "text": "It would penalize the general case, incurring an additional branch",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": " ",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "on every access.",
                            "style": "Plain"
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Vec",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " will never automatically shrink itself, even if completely empty. This",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "ensures no unnecessary allocations or deallocations occur. Emptying a ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Vec",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "and then filling it back up to the same ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "len",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/vec/struct.Vec.html#method.len"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " should incur no calls to",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "the allocator. If you wish to free up unused memory, use",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "shrink_to_fit",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/vec/struct.Vec.html#method.shrink_to_fit"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " or ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "shrink_to",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/vec/struct.Vec.html#method.shrink_to"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ".",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "push",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/vec/struct.Vec.html#method.push"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " and ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "insert",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/vec/struct.Vec.html#method.insert"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " will never (re)allocate if the reported capacity is",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "sufficient. ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "push",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/vec/struct.Vec.html#method.push"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " and ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "insert",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/vec/struct.Vec.html#method.insert"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "will",
                    "style": "Emphasis"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " (re)allocate if",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "len",
                    "style": "Plain",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/vec/struct.Vec.html#method.len"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " == ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "capacity",
                    "style": "Plain",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/vec/struct.Vec.html#method.capacity"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ". That is, the reported capacity is completely",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "accurate, and can be relied on. It can even be used to manually free the memory",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "allocated by a ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Vec",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " if desired. Bulk insertion methods ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "may",
                    "style": "Emphasis"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " reallocate, even",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "when not necessary.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Vec",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " does not guarantee any particular growth strategy when reallocating",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "when full, nor when ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "reserve",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/vec/struct.Vec.html#method.reserve"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " is called. The current strategy is basic",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "and it may prove desirable to use a non-constant growth factor. Whatever",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "strategy is used will of course guarantee ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "O",
                    "style": "Emphasis"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "(1) amortized ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "push",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/vec/struct.Vec.html#method.push"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ".",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "It is guaranteed, in order to respect the intentions of the programmer, that",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "all of ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "vec![e_1, e_2, ..., e_n]",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "vec![x; n]",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", and ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Vec::with_capacity(n)",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/vec/struct.Vec.html#method.with_capacity"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " produce a ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Vec",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "that requests an allocation of the exact size needed for precisely ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "n",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " elements from the allocator,",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "and no other size (such as, for example: a size rounded up to the nearest power of 2).",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "The allocator will return an allocation that is at least as large as requested, but it may be larger.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "It is guaranteed that the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Vec::capacity",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/vec/struct.Vec.html#method.capacity"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " method returns a value that is at least the requested capacity",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "and not more than the allocated capacity.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "The method ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Vec::shrink_to_fit",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/vec/struct.Vec.html#method.shrink_to_fit"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " will attempt to discard excess capacity an allocator has given to a ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Vec",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ".",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "If ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "len",
                    "style": "Plain",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/vec/struct.Vec.html#method.len"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " == ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "capacity",
                    "style": "Plain",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/vec/struct.Vec.html#method.capacity"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", then a ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Vec<T>",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " can be converted",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "to and from a ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Box<[T]>",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/boxed/struct.Box.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " without reallocating or moving the elements.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Vec",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " exploits this fact as much as reasonable when implementing common conversions",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "such as ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "into_boxed_slice",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/vec/struct.Vec.html#method.into_boxed_slice"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ".",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Vec",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " will not specifically overwrite any data that is removed from it,",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "but also won't specifically preserve it. Its uninitialized memory is",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "scratch space that it may use however it wants. It will generally just do",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "whatever is most efficient or otherwise easy to implement. Do not rely on",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "removed data to be erased for security purposes. Even if you drop a ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Vec",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", its",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "buffer may simply be reused by another allocation. Even if you zero a ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Vec",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "'s memory",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "first, that might not actually happen because the optimizer does not consider",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "this a side-effect that must be preserved. There is one case which we will",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "not break, however: using ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "unsafe",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " code to write to the excess capacity,",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "and then increasing the length to match, is always valid.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Currently, ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Vec",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " does not guarantee the order in which elements are dropped.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "The order has changed in the past and may change again.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
            "level": "SingleLine"
          }
        ]
