              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Violating these may cause problems like corrupting the allocator's",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "internal data structures. For example it is ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "not",
                    "style": "Strong"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " safe",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "to build a ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Vec<u8>",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " from a pointer to a C ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "char",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " array with length ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "size_t",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ".",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "It's also not safe to build one from a ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Vec<u16>",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " and its length, because",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "the allocator cares about the alignment, and these two types have different",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "alignments. The buffer was allocated with alignment 2 (for ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "u16",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "), but after",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "turning it into a ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Vec<u8>",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " it'll be deallocated with alignment 1.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
