      {
        "path": "Vec::as_ptr",
        "kind": "function",
        "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/vec/struct.Vec.html#method.as_ptr",
        "docs": [
          {
            "type": "truncatedBlock",
            "nodes": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Returns a raw pointer to the vector's buffer, or a dangling raw pointer",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "valid for zero sized reads if the vector didn't allocate.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "The caller must ensure that the vector outlives the pointer this",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "function returns, or else it will end up dangling.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Modifying the vector may cause its buffer to be reallocated,",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "which would also make any pointers to it invalid.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "The caller must also ensure that the memory the pointer (non-transitively) points to",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "is never written to (except inside an ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "UnsafeCell",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ") using this pointer or any pointer",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "derived from it. If you need to mutate the contents of the slice, use ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "as_mut_ptr",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/vec/struct.Vec.html#method.as_mut_ptr"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ".",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "This method guarantees that for the purpose of the aliasing model, this method",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "does not materialize a reference to the underlying slice, and thus the returned pointer",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "will remain valid when mixed with other calls to ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "as_ptr",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/vec/struct.Vec.html#method.as_ptr"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "as_mut_ptr",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/vec/struct.Vec.html#method.as_mut_ptr"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ",",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "and ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "as_non_null",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/vec/struct.Vec.html#method.as_non_null"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ".",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Note that calling other methods that materialize mutable references to the slice,",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "or mutable references to specific elements you are planning on accessing through this pointer,",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "as well as writing to those elements, may still invalidate this pointer.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "See the second example below for how this guarantee can be used.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Title",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Examples",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "let x = vec![1, 2, 4];\nlet x_ptr = x.as_ptr();\n\nunsafe {\n    for i in 0..x.len() {\n        assert_eq!(*x_ptr.add(i), 1 << i);\n    }\n}"
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Due to the aliasing guarantee, the following code is legal:",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "unsafe {\n    let mut v = vec![0, 1, 2];\n    let ptr1 = v.as_ptr();\n    let _ = ptr1.read();\n    let ptr2 = v.as_mut_ptr().offset(2);\n    ptr2.write(2);\n    // Notably, the write to `ptr2` did *not* invalidate `ptr1`\n    // because it mutated a different element:\n    let _ = ptr1.read();\n}"
              }
            ],
            "level": "SingleLine"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "path": "Vec::as_mut_ptr",
        "kind": "function",
        "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/vec/struct.Vec.html#method.as_mut_ptr",
        "docs": [
          {
            "type": "truncatedBlock",
            "nodes": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Returns a raw mutable pointer to the vector's buffer, or a dangling",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "raw pointer valid for zero sized reads if the vector didn't allocate.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "The caller must ensure that the vector outlives the pointer this",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "function returns, or else it will end up dangling.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Modifying the vector may cause its buffer to be reallocated,",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "which would also make any pointers to it invalid.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "This method guarantees that for the purpose of the aliasing model, this method",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "does not materialize a reference to the underlying slice, and thus the returned pointer",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "will remain valid when mixed with other calls to ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "as_ptr",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/vec/struct.Vec.html#method.as_ptr"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "as_mut_ptr",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/vec/struct.Vec.html#method.as_mut_ptr"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ",",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "and ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "as_non_null",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/vec/struct.Vec.html#method.as_non_null"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ".",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Note that calling other methods that materialize references to the slice,",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "or references to specific elements you are planning on accessing through this pointer,",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "may still invalidate this pointer.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "See the second example below for how this guarantee can be used.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "The method also guarantees that, as long as ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "T",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " is not zero-sized and the capacity is",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "nonzero, the pointer may be passed into ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "dealloc",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/alloc/GlobalAlloc/index.html?search=alloc%3A%3Aalloc%3A%3AGlobalAlloc%3A%3Adealloc"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " with a layout of",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Layout::array::<T>(capacity)",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " in order to deallocate the backing memory. If this is done,",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "be careful not to run the destructor of the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Vec",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", as dropping it will result in",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "double-frees. Wrapping the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Vec",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " in a ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "ManuallyDrop",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/mem/manually_drop/index.html?search=core%3A%3Amem%3A%3Amanually%5Fdrop%3A%3AManuallyDrop"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " is the typical way to achieve this.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Title",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Examples",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "// Allocate vector big enough for 4 elements.\nlet size = 4;\nlet mut x: Vec<i32> = Vec::with_capacity(size);\nlet x_ptr = x.as_mut_ptr();\n\n// Initialize elements via raw pointer writes, then set length.\nunsafe {\n    for i in 0..size {\n        *x_ptr.add(i) = i as i32;\n    }\n    x.set_len(size);\n}\nassert_eq!(&*x, &[0, 1, 2, 3]);"
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Due to the aliasing guarantee, the following code is legal:",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "unsafe {\n    let mut v = vec![0];\n    let ptr1 = v.as_mut_ptr();\n    ptr1.write(1);\n    let ptr2 = v.as_mut_ptr();\n    ptr2.write(2);\n    // Notably, the write to `ptr2` did *not* invalidate `ptr1`:\n    ptr1.write(3);\n}"
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Deallocating a vector using ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Box",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/boxed/struct.Box.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " (which uses ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "dealloc",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/alloc/GlobalAlloc/index.html?search=alloc%3A%3Aalloc%3A%3AGlobalAlloc%3A%3Adealloc"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " internally):",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "use std::mem::{ManuallyDrop, MaybeUninit};\n\nlet mut v = ManuallyDrop::new(vec![0, 1, 2]);\nlet ptr = v.as_mut_ptr();\nlet capacity = v.capacity();\nlet slice_ptr: *mut [MaybeUninit<i32>] =\n    std::ptr::slice_from_raw_parts_mut(ptr.cast(), capacity);\ndrop(unsafe { Box::from_raw(slice_ptr) });"
              }
            ],
            "level": "SingleLine"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "path": "Vec::as_non_null",
        "kind": "function",
        "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/vec/struct.Vec.html#method.as_non_null",
        "docs": [
          {
            "type": "truncatedBlock",
            "nodes": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Returns a ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "NonNull",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " pointer to the vector's buffer, or a dangling",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "NonNull",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " pointer valid for zero sized reads if the vector didn't allocate.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "The caller must ensure that the vector outlives the pointer this",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "function returns, or else it will end up dangling.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Modifying the vector may cause its buffer to be reallocated,",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "which would also make any pointers to it invalid.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "This method guarantees that for the purpose of the aliasing model, this method",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "does not materialize a reference to the underlying slice, and thus the returned pointer",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "will remain valid when mixed with other calls to ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "as_ptr",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/vec/struct.Vec.html#method.as_ptr"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "as_mut_ptr",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/vec/struct.Vec.html#method.as_mut_ptr"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ",",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "and ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "as_non_null",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/vec/struct.Vec.html#method.as_non_null"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ".",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Note that calling other methods that materialize references to the slice,",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "or references to specific elements you are planning on accessing through this pointer,",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "may still invalidate this pointer.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "See the second example below for how this guarantee can be used.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Title",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Examples",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "#![feature(box_vec_non_null)]\n\n// Allocate vector big enough for 4 elements.\nlet size = 4;\nlet mut x: Vec<i32> = Vec::with_capacity(size);\nlet x_ptr = x.as_non_null();\n\n// Initialize elements via raw pointer writes, then set length.\nunsafe {\n    for i in 0..size {\n        x_ptr.add(i).write(i as i32);\n    }\n    x.set_len(size);\n}\nassert_eq!(&*x, &[0, 1, 2, 3]);"
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Due to the aliasing guarantee, the following code is legal:",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "#![feature(box_vec_non_null)]\n\nunsafe {\n    let mut v = vec![0];\n    let ptr1 = v.as_non_null();\n    ptr1.write(1);\n    let ptr2 = v.as_non_null();\n    ptr2.write(2);\n    // Notably, the write to `ptr2` did *not* invalidate `ptr1`:\n    ptr1.write(3);\n}"
              }
            ],
            "level": "SingleLine"
          }
        ]
      },
