      {
        "path": "Vec::drain",
        "kind": "function",
        "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/vec/struct.Vec.html#method.drain",
        "docs": [
          {
            "type": "truncatedBlock",
            "nodes": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Removes the subslice indicated by the given range from the vector,",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "returning a double-ended iterator over the removed subslice.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "If the iterator is dropped before being fully consumed,",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "it drops the remaining removed elements.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "The returned iterator keeps a mutable borrow on the vector to optimize",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "its implementation.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Title",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Panics",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Panics if the range has ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "start_bound > end_bound",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", or, if the range is",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "bounded on either end and past the length of the vector.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Title",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Leaking",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "If the returned iterator goes out of scope without being dropped (due to",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "mem::forget",
                    "style": "InlineCode",
                    "url": "https://doc.rust-lang.org/nightly/core/mem/index.html?search=core%3A%3Amem%3A%3Aforget"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", for example), the vector may have lost and leaked",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "elements arbitrarily, including elements outside the range.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Title",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Examples",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "let mut v = vec![1, 2, 3];\nlet u: Vec<_> = v.drain(1..).collect();\nassert_eq!(v, &[1]);\nassert_eq!(u, &[2, 3]);\n\n// A full range clears the vector, like `clear()` does\nv.drain(..);\nassert_eq!(v, &[]);"
              }
            ],
            "level": "SingleLine"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "path": "Vec::clear",
        "kind": "function",
        "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/vec/struct.Vec.html#method.clear",
        "docs": [
          {
            "type": "truncatedBlock",
            "nodes": [
