      {
        "path": "Vec::leak",
        "kind": "function",
        "url": "http://docs.rust-lang.org/nightly/alloc/vec/struct.Vec.html#method.leak",
        "docs": [
          {
            "type": "truncatedBlock",
            "nodes": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Consumes and leaks the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Vec",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", returning a mutable reference to the contents,",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "&'a mut [T]",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ".",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Note that the type ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "T",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " must outlive the chosen lifetime ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "'a",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ". If the type",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "has only static references, or none at all, then this may be chosen to be",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "'static",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ".",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "As of Rust 1.57, this method does not reallocate or shrink the ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Vec",
                    "style": "InlineCode"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ",",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "so the leaked allocation may include unused capacity that is not part",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "of the returned slice.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "This function is mainly useful for data that lives for the remainder of",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "the program's life. Dropping the returned reference will cause a memory",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "leak.",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "heading",
                "level": "Title",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Examples",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "spans": [
                  {
                    "text": "Simple usage:",
                    "style": "Plain"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "codeBlock",
                "lang": "rust",
                "code": "let x = vec![1, 2, 3];\nlet static_ref: &'static mut [usize] = x.leak();\nstatic_ref[0] += 1;\nassert_eq!(static_ref, &[2, 2, 3]);"
              }
            ],
            "level": "SingleLine"
          }
        ]
